w: 1.~The day _ Thou ga- _ vest, Lord, _ is end- ed, The dark- ness falls _ at Thy be- hest; To Thee _ our morn- _ ing hymns _ a- scen- ded, Thy praise _ shall sanc- _ ti- fy _ our rest.
w: 2.~We thank _ Thee that _ Thy church, _ un- slee- ping, While earth rolls on- _ ward in- to light, Through all _ the world _ her watch _ is keep- ing, And rests _ not now _ by day _ or night.
w: 3.~As o’er _ each con- _ ti- nent _ and is- land The dawn leads on _ a- no- ther day, The voice _ of prayer _ is ne- _ ver si- lent, Nor dies _ the strain _ of praise _ a- way.
w: 4.~The sun _ that bids _ us rest _ is wa- king Our breth- ren ’neath _ the we- stern sky, And hour _ by hour _ fresh lips _ are mak- ing Thy won- _ drous do- _ ings heard _ on high.
w: 5.~So be _ it, Lord; _ Thy throne _ shall ne- ver, Like earth’s proud em- _ pires, pass a- way: Thy king- _ dom stands, _ and grows _ for- ev- er, Till all _ Thy crea- _ tures own _ Thy sway.
